	(text "J17 SERVO UART: same pinout as CN13 on the MES2 Harvester.\nJ15 SERVO 24V: pin 1 = +24 V like every power terminal here\n(Harvester CN5 is reversed: re-pin that cable).\nThe FE-URT-2 turns the UART into the Feetech half-duplex\nservo bus and passes the 24 V on to the servos.\nUART on module USART2: PA2 TX → pin 4,\npin 3 → PA3 RX (5 V-tolerant). R36 / R37 10k\npull-ups keep RX / TX idle HIGH (TX floats in reset).\nSet the FE-URT-2 level switch to 3.3 V (not 5 V):\nit only sets the UART levels, the servo 24 V is\nunchanged. At 5 V its TX exceeds PA3's limit while\nthe module is unpowered and back-feeds the 3V3 via R36.\nF9 3 A PTC on the servo 24 V. F10 1.1 A PTC on the\nFE-URT-2 5 V, fed from the screen converter so a\nservo-side short can't pull down the module supply.\n24 V only for 24 V servo types.\nBlank chip: the ST bootloader probes PA2 / PA3, so flash\nover SWD first (the normal flow)."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 294.64 198.12 0)
		(effects (font (size 1.27 1.27)) (justify left top))
		(uuid "3e18fcd4-13d8-555f-85b1-4df8d0c68f07")
	)
	(text "FE-URT-2 mount: H6-H9 M3 x 2 mm SMD standoffs (SMTSOM320BTR)\non its 48.5 x 28.7 mm holes, M3 screws from the top. No parts under it.\nStandoffs not connected."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 210.82 226.06 0)
		(effects (font (size 1.27 1.27)) (justify left top))
		(uuid "d86bf803-0de8-5912-9aa9-0029a8a221ee")
	)
